From 18f4ca0b57f3291b3d91f94c04528c37120c5f19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ravindu644 <droidcasts@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:03:29 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] hybris: vulkan: emulate dma-buf export through dma-heap
 imports

The Mali driver advertises VK_KHR_external_memory_fd and
VK_EXT_external_memory_dma_buf, but only imports dma-bufs, and only into
buffers; vkGetMemoryFdKHR returns VK_SUCCESS without writing the fd. Zink
needs export for every GBM buffer (Xwayland glamor) and for X11 clients
presenting through DRI3.

Allocate exportable memory from /dev/dma_heap/system (HYBRIS_VK_DMA_HEAP)
and import it, which the driver renders into correctly, then hand out
duplicates of our fd. Imported dma-bufs are tracked too, because Zink
re-exports them for implicit sync. External-memory create info is stripped
from images and buffers, and the capability queries report export and
import.

Signed-off-by: ravindu644 <droidcasts@protonmail.com>
---
 hybris/vulkan/vulkan.c | 335 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 325 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

